1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,014
Hi! Let's count Fibonacci numbers, and watch each new number take shape.

2
00:00:05,614 --> 00:00:09,145
We start with zero and one. These are our two starting values.

3
00:00:09,745 --> 00:00:14,660
To make the next number, add the previous two. Then use the newest pair, and do it again.

4
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:21,346
The small labels tell us each number's place. We start at F zero, so F two is the third entry.

5
00:00:21,946 --> 00:00:27,359
The older value sits on the left. The newer value sits beside it. Their labels move with them.

6
00:00:27,959 --> 00:00:33,889
Listen for plus and equals. The answer appears when we say its name, and becomes our newest value.

7
00:00:34,489 --> 00:00:42,462
Number windows show values, not piles of things. A window marked one thousand stands for that value, not one thousand objects.

8
00:00:43,062 --> 00:00:49,763
We'll keep adding until the sequence first passes one hundred million. The numbers grow, but the rule stays the same.

9
00:00:50,363 --> 00:00:50,942
zero

10
00:00:52,942 --> 00:00:53,430
one

11
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,906
zero plus one equals

12
00:00:57,066 --> 00:00:57,554
one

13
00:00:58,154 --> 00:01:03,650
There are two ones in a row. One is a starting value; the next was made by adding zero and one.

14
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:10,366
They have the same value, but different places. Keep both entries, because each belongs to the sequence.

15
00:01:12,966 --> 00:01:14,301
one plus one equals

16
00:01:14,461 --> 00:01:14,977
two

17
00:01:16,977 --> 00:01:18,249
one plus two equals

18
00:01:18,409 --> 00:01:18,967
three

19
00:01:20,967 --> 00:01:22,335
two plus three equals

20
00:01:22,495 --> 00:01:23,096
five

21
00:01:25,096 --> 00:01:26,507
three plus five equals

22
00:01:26,667 --> 00:01:27,179
eight

23
00:01:29,179 --> 00:01:30,630
five plus eight equals

24
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:31,481
thirteen

25
00:01:33,481 --> 00:01:34,962
eight plus thirteen equals

26
00:01:35,122 --> 00:01:35,838
twenty-one

27
00:01:36,438 --> 00:01:43,998
Let's look inside that addition. In the ones column, eight plus three makes eleven: one stays here, and one ten moves left.

28
00:01:44,598 --> 00:01:52,037
That carried ten joins the ten already there. The columns now show two tens and one one. Then the newest pair moves on.

29
00:01:54,637 --> 00:01:56,463
thirteen plus twenty-one equals

30
00:01:56,623 --> 00:01:57,341
thirty-four

31
00:01:59,341 --> 00:02:01,436
twenty-one plus thirty-four equals

32
00:02:01,596 --> 00:02:02,452
fifty-five

33
00:02:04,452 --> 00:02:06,446
thirty-four plus fifty-five equals

34
00:02:06,606 --> 00:02:07,374
eighty-nine

35
00:02:09,374 --> 00:02:11,374
fifty-five plus eighty-nine equals

36
00:02:11,534 --> 00:02:12,871
one hundred forty-four

37
00:02:14,871 --> 00:02:17,588
eighty-nine plus one hundred forty-four equals

38
00:02:17,748 --> 00:02:19,025
two hundred thirty-three

39
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:25,619
Here the ones make thirteen. Write three and carry one ten. The tens, including that carry, also make thirteen.

40
00:02:26,219 --> 00:02:33,273
Write three tens, and carry one hundred. That hundred joins the hundred already there. Every column keeps its own place.

41
00:02:35,873 --> 00:02:39,141
one hundred forty-four plus two hundred thirty-three equals

42
00:02:39,301 --> 00:02:40,795
three hundred seventy-seven

43
00:02:42,795 --> 00:02:46,367
two hundred thirty-three plus three hundred seventy-seven equals

44
00:02:46,527 --> 00:02:47,591
six hundred ten

45
00:02:49,591 --> 00:02:52,921
three hundred seventy-seven plus six hundred ten equals

46
00:02:53,081 --> 00:02:54,576
nine hundred eighty-seven

47
00:02:56,576 --> 00:02:59,909
six hundred ten plus nine hundred eighty-seven equals

48
00:03:00,069 --> 00:03:02,369
one thousand five hundred ninety-seven

49
00:03:04,369 --> 00:03:08,923
nine hundred eighty-seven plus one thousand five hundred ninety-seven equals

50
00:03:09,083 --> 00:03:11,075
two thousand five hundred eighty-four

51
00:03:11,675 --> 00:03:18,707
Now the values reach into the thousands. Start at the ones and follow each carry to the next column, one place at a time.

52
00:03:19,307 --> 00:03:28,150
Seven plus seven makes fourteen. Next come eighteen tens, then fifteen hundreds. Each carry moves one column left; it never skips a place.

53
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:35,786
one thousand five hundred ninety-seven plus two thousand five hundred eighty-four equals

54
00:03:35,946 --> 00:03:37,806
four thousand one hundred eighty-one

55
00:03:39,806 --> 00:03:44,630
two thousand five hundred eighty-four plus four thousand one hundred eighty-one equals

56
00:03:44,790 --> 00:03:47,055
six thousand seven hundred sixty-five

57
00:03:49,055 --> 00:03:54,151
four thousand one hundred eighty-one plus six thousand seven hundred sixty-five equals

58
00:03:54,311 --> 00:03:56,368
ten thousand nine hundred forty-six

59
00:03:58,368 --> 00:04:03,773
six thousand seven hundred sixty-five plus ten thousand nine hundred forty-six equals

60
00:04:03,933 --> 00:04:06,229
seventeen thousand seven hundred eleven

61
00:04:08,229 --> 00:04:13,532
ten thousand nine hundred forty-six plus seventeen thousand seven hundred eleven equals

62
00:04:13,692 --> 00:04:16,047
twenty-eight thousand six hundred fifty-seven

63
00:04:18,047 --> 00:04:23,828
seventeen thousand seven hundred eleven plus twenty-eight thousand six hundred fifty-seven equals

64
00:04:23,988 --> 00:04:26,252
forty-six thousand three hundred sixty-eight

65
00:04:28,252 --> 00:04:34,130
twenty-eight thousand six hundred fifty-seven plus forty-six thousand three hundred sixty-eight equals

66
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:36,112
seventy-five thousand twenty-five

67
00:04:38,112 --> 00:04:43,394
forty-six thousand three hundred sixty-eight plus seventy-five thousand twenty-five equals

68
00:04:43,554 --> 00:04:46,392
one hundred twenty-one thousand three hundred ninety-three

69
00:04:46,992 --> 00:04:54,332
The commas help us read groups of three digits. They are separators, not extra digits, and they do not change the addition.

70
00:04:54,932 --> 00:05:02,052
Keep the ones columns lined up on the right. Even with larger numbers, each column still adds the same kind of units.

71
00:05:04,652 --> 00:05:10,598
seventy-five thousand twenty-five plus one hundred twenty-one thousand three hundred ninety-three equals

72
00:05:10,758 --> 00:05:13,409
one hundred ninety-six thousand four hundred eighteen

73
00:05:15,409 --> 00:05:22,208
one hundred twenty-one thousand three hundred ninety-three plus one hundred ninety-six thousand four hundred eighteen equals

74
00:05:22,368 --> 00:05:25,080
three hundred seventeen thousand eight hundred eleven

75
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:33,610
one hundred ninety-six thousand four hundred eighteen plus three hundred seventeen thousand eight hundred eleven equals

76
00:05:33,770 --> 00:05:36,526
five hundred fourteen thousand two hundred twenty-nine

77
00:05:38,526 --> 00:05:45,398
three hundred seventeen thousand eight hundred eleven plus five hundred fourteen thousand two hundred twenty-nine equals

78
00:05:45,558 --> 00:05:47,528
eight hundred thirty-two thousand forty

79
00:05:49,528 --> 00:05:55,432
five hundred fourteen thousand two hundred twenty-nine plus eight hundred thirty-two thousand forty equals

80
00:05:55,592 --> 00:05:59,269
one million three hundred forty-six thousand two hundred sixty-nine

81
00:06:01,269 --> 00:06:08,111
eight hundred thirty-two thousand forty plus one million three hundred forty-six thousand two hundred sixty-nine equals

82
00:06:08,271 --> 00:06:11,501
two million one hundred seventy-eight thousand three hundred nine

83
00:06:13,501 --> 00:06:21,830
one million three hundred forty-six thousand two hundred sixty-nine plus two million one hundred seventy-eight thousand three hundred nine equals

84
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:26,070
three million five hundred twenty-four thousand five hundred seventy-eight

85
00:06:28,070 --> 00:06:36,722
two million one hundred seventy-eight thousand three hundred nine plus three million five hundred twenty-four thousand five hundred seventy-eight equals

86
00:06:36,882 --> 00:06:40,597
five million seven hundred two thousand eight hundred eighty-seven

87
00:06:42,597 --> 00:06:51,654
three million five hundred twenty-four thousand five hundred seventy-eight plus five million seven hundred two thousand eight hundred eighty-seven equals

88
00:06:51,814 --> 00:06:55,798
nine million two hundred twenty-seven thousand four hundred sixty-five

89
00:06:57,798 --> 00:07:06,541
five million seven hundred two thousand eight hundred eighty-seven plus nine million two hundred twenty-seven thousand four hundred sixty-five equals

90
00:07:06,701 --> 00:07:10,446
fourteen million nine hundred thirty thousand three hundred fifty-two

91
00:07:12,446 --> 00:07:21,244
nine million two hundred twenty-seven thousand four hundred sixty-five plus fourteen million nine hundred thirty thousand three hundred fifty-two equals

92
00:07:21,404 --> 00:07:25,624
twenty-four million one hundred fifty-seven thousand eight hundred seventeen

93
00:07:27,624 --> 00:07:36,852
fourteen million nine hundred thirty thousand three hundred fifty-two plus twenty-four million one hundred fifty-seven thousand eight hundred seventeen equals

94
00:07:37,012 --> 00:07:40,116
thirty-nine million eighty-eight thousand one hundred sixty-nine

95
00:07:42,116 --> 00:07:50,876
twenty-four million one hundred fifty-seven thousand eight hundred seventeen plus thirty-nine million eighty-eight thousand one hundred sixty-nine equals

96
00:07:51,036 --> 00:07:55,116
sixty-three million two hundred forty-five thousand nine hundred eighty-six

97
00:07:55,716 --> 00:08:02,574
We have reached the final pair for this journey. Both values are below one hundred million. Their sum will cross that mark.

98
00:08:03,174 --> 00:08:11,158
Watch the labels as the two values enter the formula. It is the same addition we used at the start, with more place-value columns.

99
00:08:13,758 --> 00:08:22,520
thirty-nine million eighty-eight thousand one hundred sixty-nine plus sixty-three million two hundred forty-five thousand nine hundred eighty-six equals

100
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:27,274
one hundred two million three hundred thirty-four thousand one hundred fifty-five

101
00:08:27,874 --> 00:08:35,744
We've counted forty-one entries, from F zero through F forty. Two starting values, then thirty-nine additions brought us here.

102
00:08:36,344 --> 00:08:43,028
The newest number is just past one hundred million. We stop here today, but the rule can keep making more numbers.

103
00:08:43,628 --> 00:08:51,475
Remember the motion: take the previous two, add them, keep the newest pair, and repeat. Every new entry has a place in the chain.

104
00:08:52,075 --> 00:08:54,439
Thanks for counting with me. See you next time!
